Main findings for the writer:
- Novelty survives WITH REWORDING. Known: max/OR = standard multi-instance assumption (dietterich1997solving, hoffmann2011knowledge); pair-conditioned inputs (lee2020biobert, zhong2021frustratingly); finer supervision helping a coarse "contains any" decision (rei2019jointly, dasanmartino2019fine); instance-supervised models as the MIL upper bound (li2021dual); sentence filters give poor pair precision (pyysalo2008comparative, lim2016minter: abstract AUC 0.97 but species-pair precision 25%). Not found anywhere: varying only the question put to the LLM teacher (pair vs sentence) with the same passages/encoder, pair student trained on no sentence labels, compared on the sentence decision.
- Counter-evidence to cite and scope around: magge2021deepademiner (span tagger loses to tweet classifier), mraz2026fewshot (arXiv; per-pair LLM prompting not dominant), hu2025decomposition, pavlopoulos2022from (attribution can localise, so say "only the pair verifier is TRAINED to say which pair").
Caveats:
- On BioRED the sentence label is the OR of gold pair labels, so a pair win is expected there; the biodiversity human SENTENCE labels are the real test. "Same teacher" applies to biodiversity arms only.
- 0.724 and all our numbers come from CONTEXT.md (sandbox, silver labels); recheck against ANALYSIS.md.
- Do not quote: Riedel's 13% (its own table averages 16.7%); Gao's "32% N/A"/"53%"; SummaC's 73.5% as max/mean; Zaidan's "more fruitful" as a finding; Keck's 89.5% as accuracy (it is precision).
- Abstract-only entries: herrerozazo2013ddi, gurulingappa2012development. Read through a rendering tool, near-verbatim: lim2016minter, thieu2012literature. Only the arXiv version was read: dumitrache2018crowdsourcing. mraz2026fewshot is a preprint; recheck before camera-ready.
- BiotXplorer: application only; say only what its public BISS abstract says (pair-in-passage evaluations, 31%/85%, multi-species error cause); nothing about a working relationship, internals, roadmap or its authors' forthcoming paper.
Open problems: no published share of negative pairs inside interaction-positive sentences (could be computed from public PPI corpora); a soft-aggregator check and a sentence-classifier attribution baseline would pre-empt two reviewer questions.
